cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use RippleTwin in your work, please cite it using the metadata in this file."
type: software
title: "RippleTwin"
abstract: >-
  RippleTwin is a digital twin of the Melbourne CBD for temporary traffic
  management. A planner places the barriers, signs and variable message signs
  for a road closure and sees the effect on queues, delay, detours, trams,
  buses and pedestrians before deployment. A language model reads the signs
  as four types of road user would, a deterministic in-browser engine computes
  the traffic impacts from open data, and Eclipse SUMO cross-checks the main
  scenario on the real street network. Built by Team Uncapped at the FEIT
  Hackathon Festival 2026 (University of Melbourne), where it won the RPM Hire
  Prize.
authors:
  - name: "Team Uncapped"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Zemmeng/rippletwin"
url: "https://hackathon-site.zemmmeng.workers.dev/web/public/"
license: MIT
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-01"
keywords:
  - digital twin
  - traffic simulation
  - temporary traffic management
  - road closure
  - variable message signs
  - large language models
  - Eclipse SUMO
  - Cloudflare Workers
  - open data
  - Melbourne
